// A self-referential MAP arm with no `null` traps the COMPILER at the declaration alone — no
// `is`, no binding, no value of type T. A `null` arm MASKS it, which is the opposite polarity
// from D982/D985, so no single witness can see both. Mutual recursion runs; direct
// self-reference is required. See D984.
// Should print ok.
type T = string | {[string]: T}

print("ok")
